{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        new Main().run();\n    }\n\n    private void run() {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n = sc.nextInt();\n        String s = sc.next();\n        sc.close();\n        \n        int nk = 0, nv = 0, no = 0;\n        int[] kpos = new int[n];\n        int[] vpos = new int[n];\n        int[] opos = new int[n];\n        \n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            char c = s.charAt(i);\n            if (c == 'K') kpos[nk++] = i;\n            else if (c == 'V') vpos[nv++] = i;\n            else opos[no++] = i;\n        }\n        \n        int[] snk = new int[n + 1];\n        int[] snv = new int[n + 1];\n        int[] sno = new int[n + 1];\n        \n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            char c = s.charAt(i);\n            snk[i + 1] = snk[i] + (c == 'K' ? 1 : 0);\n            snv[i + 1] = snv[i] + (c == 'V' ? 1 : 0);\n            sno[i + 1] = sno[i] + (c == 'O' ? 1 : 0);\n        }\n        \n        final int INF = (int)1e9;\n        int[][][][] dp = new int[2][nk + 1][nv + 1][no + 1];\n        \n        for (int[][][] a : dp) {\n            for (int[][] b : a) {\n                for (int[] c : b) {\n                    Arrays.fill(c, INF);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        \n        dp[0][0][0][0] = 0;\n        \n        for (int k = 0; k <= nk; k++) {\n            for (int v = 0; v <= nv; v++) {\n                for (int o = 0; o <= no; o++) {\n                    for (int hv = 0; hv < 2; hv++) {\n                        int cur = dp[hv][k][v][o];\n                        if (cur == INF) continue;\n                        \n                        if (k < nk && hv == 0) {\n                            int cost = Math.max(snv[kpos[k]] - v, 0) + Math.max(sno[kpos[k]] - o, 0);\n                            dp[0][k + 1][v][o] = Math.min(dp[0][k + 1][v][o], cur + cost);\n                        }\n                        if (v < nv) {\n                            int cost = Math.max(snk[vpos[v]] - k, 0) + Math.max(sno[vpos[v]] - o, 0);\n                            dp[1][k][v + 1][o] = Math.min(dp[1][k][v + 1][o], cur + cost);\n                        }\n                        if (o < no) {\n                            int cost = Math.max(snv[opos[o]] - v, 0) + Math.max(snk[opos[o]] - k, 0);\n                            dp[0][k][v][o + 1] = Math.min(dp[0][k][v][o + 1], cur + cost);\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        \n        int ans = Math.min(dp[0][nk][nv][no], dp[1][nk][nv][no]);\n        System.out.println(ans);\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nimport array\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    n = int(data[0])\n    s = data[1]\n    \n    nk = 0\n    nv = 0\n    no = 0\n    kpos = [0] * n\n    vpos = [0] * n\n    opos = [0] * n\n    \n    for i in r